    "description": "A Read(./.env) deny rule in settings.json blocks Claude Code's file-reading tools from your .env, including cat, head and tail, and also blocks Edit and Write on that file. Claude Code checks deny before ask and allow; an allow rule can't carve out an exception. The documented limit: scripts that open files themselves aren't covered.",
    "companion_text": "More Claude workflows, step by step: follow Promptwerk. Based on the Claude Code docs (Permissions, CLI reference), retrieved 2026-11-01. The editor and terminal are an animation, not a screen recording. Limits per the docs: Read and Edit deny rules apply to the built-in file tools, recognized Bash commands like cat, head and tail, and redirects. They don't apply to scripts (say, Python or Node) that open files themselves, or to commands like grep -r that don't name the file. For OS-level enforcement, turn on the sandbox. A Read rule doesn't cover NotebookEdit; add an Edit deny rule for that.",
    "hashtags": [
      "claudecode",
      "security",
      "aiworkflow",
      "coding",
      "developers"
    ],
    "short_title": "Deny-Regeln"
